  "text": "We found that 28.9% of patients experienced postoperative pulmonary complications and 12.6% experienced cardiac complications classified as Clavien–Dindo grade ≥ II. These rates are higher compared to the previous studies reporting 10–15.4% for pulmonary complications in elderly patients undergoing lung resection [9, 10]. Similary, Calado et al. [11] reported lower cardiac complications rates (8.2%) compared to our findings. In contrast, Srisomboon et al. [12] reported higher rate of respiratory (25%) and lower rates of cardiac complications (6%) in elderly patients undergoing thoracoscopic surgery."
